meta {
  name: Create Request - duplicate
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

post {
  url: {{apiUrl}}/requests
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{idToken2}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "sessionId": "{{sessionId}}"
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 409
  res.body.success: eq false
  res.body.error.code: eq DUPLICATE_REQUEST
}

docs {
  Implemented (D3). Run **Create Request** first (as the player), then this, as the
  **same player** -- a duplicate only exists if it's the same `PK`+`SK`
  (`SESSION#<id>` / `REQUEST#USER#<playerId>`), so this must use `{{idToken2}}`, not the
  host's token.

  `request.repository.ts`'s `create()` catches `ConditionalCheckFailedException` from the
  `attribute_not_exists(PK) AND attribute_not_exists(SK)` write and throws
  `DuplicateRequestError` -> 409. This specific path works correctly.

  **Known gap elsewhere in the same `catch` block:** it only handles
  `ConditionalCheckFailedException` -- any *other* error (throttling, a network blip) is
  silently swallowed with no `throw`, so `create()` would resolve successfully even though
  the write actually failed. Doesn't affect this test (a real duplicate always throws
  `ConditionalCheckFailedException`), but worth fixing with an `else throw err;`.
}
